    "turn_text": "All right, welcome everyone to our sixth edition of the Virtual Legislative Briefing Series. I'm Eric Volk, Zari Farm Bureau's Director of Public Affairs and Advocacy. Today, we're going to be having a very special guest, Congressman Jason Smith. He'll be joining us in a few minutes. And in a moment here, I'll be introducing our president, Garrett Hawkins, and he'll make some opening comments. But before that, I want to let you know how we are going to be taking questions from you today. If you are on the phone, try to get something to write with so that you can take down a number. I'm going to give you just a minute. But if you're watching on Zoom, you can just type your questions into the Q&A box down at the bottom of your screen. That's the Q&A box at the bottom of your screen. If you're watching on Facebook Live, you can just type your question into the comment area and we'll try to answer that. And then lastly, if you're listening to us on the phone, you can ask a question by texting it to us at 573-326-4501. Again, that's 573-326-4501. Just text us your question and we will try to get to it when we have an opportunity. Lastly, if there is anything that you hear today that you'd like to go back and listen to later. It's going to be available on our Facebook page. So just go to Facebook and search for Missouri Farm Bureau. The audio of the session is going to be on our digging in with Missouri Farm Bureau podcast, which you can subscribe to at mofb.org slash podcast. We'll also include a link in Monday's newsletter. If you don't already get that newsletter, you can sign up for our alerts at mofb.org slash newsletter. Now I would like to welcome Missouri Farm Bureau President Garrett Hawkins for some opening remarks.",
