  {
    "episode_id": 92294,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92294.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. Garrett, one thing you and I have talked about very frequently is like you mentioned, you know, farmers and ranchers and really any small business owner would be in this situation where you spend potentially thousands of dollars working on estate planning and then at the whim of Congress, the goalpost has moved. You may have thought you had a plan and, you know, four years later or three years later, you know, things could change pretty dramatically. That exemption level of three and a half million dollars, those were levels that were passed. They referred to that as the 2009 exemption. So those are the levels that would have been in place the first couple of years of the Obama administration. That causes a lot of uncertainty for our farm and ranch families and that's ultimately why our organization is advocating a full repeal because on principle we believe that your death is not a taxable event and we believe this is wrong.",
