    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, Garrett, and I think I heard an interesting statistic on my webinar this morning and I looked it up and it is indeed true. You mentioned framing this as a green new deal and a tax hike as being kind of like a wolf in sheep's clothing and a disguised as an infrastructure package. Did you know, I bet you might not have, that the amount of funding in the proposed American Jobs Plan for only electric vehicles is more than the amount proposed for roads, bridges, and other what we would call surface transportation infrastructure combined. I had to look that up to be sure that was true, and it is a fact. So you're exactly right. This is the administration pushing their environmental and climate agenda on all Americans, but especially farmers and ranchers. And Eric bowl. If you are on zoom Eric bowl did put in the chat box. So if you look at the I guess bottom of your screen. You'll see the link to our action center where you can tell your tax story. There's no story too big or too small and please do not be shy. We will not share any information, any personal information without your permission and say so, but as we are working to build up our arguments and really start our public awareness campaign, if you will, on this issue. Those stories, when I was working in Congress, those were the most powerful stories to tell to legislative staff and to legislators themselves. If you're watching on Facebook, in the description of this live video, you'll see the same link. So please go ahead. We'll also be sending that out in our weekly newsletter, which will come out on Monday, April 19th. Please, please, please do not be shy. If you have questions about any of these proposals or if you're just looking for somebody to talk to or somebody to give a better explanation, please do not hesitate to contact us at the home office. Garrett, I think Congressman Smith is just about to join us. Do you have any final thoughts or comments before he jumps on?",
