    "turn_text": "Well, Spencer, I will say since we've talked a little bit about infrastructure, it wouldn't be a virtual legislative briefing without mentioning broadband, right? So I'm excited to report that we'll have the chance to testify before a subcommittee of the House Transportation Committee later this month to talk about broadband and economic development. It looks like the Congressman, though, has joined us, our distinguished congressman from the 8th District, no stranger to Farm Bureau. Recipient of the Friend of Farm Bureau award every time you've been eligible Congressman. And we've spent some time teeing this up for you in terms of all things taxes. Spencer has talked about infrastructure. Congressman, it goes without saying, I've been part of a lot of these tax discussions for years. And now to hear the rhetoric morphing to, well, we are transferring too much wealth. This is about social justice. All these things that are now being factored into the discussion about tax policy It is really alarming. So I'm teeing it up for you to tell us what's the lay of the land and what should we be watching for in the days and weeks ahead. So Congressman.",
