  {
    "episode_id": 92294,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92294.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "You know, I am definitely pleased with President Biden's appointee as the USTR Trade Ambassador. I'm not necessarily usually the most positive person when it comes to the Biden administration, but I will say that he could have picked someone that would not be as helpful. And the young lady that he picked actually served on the Ways and Means Committee was the Trade Council. We know very well, and we don't agree 100%, but definitely I think will be very helpful in trying to create some of these trade agreements. Trade is typically bipartisan. And hopefully it will continue to go that way because we're all fighting for American farmers and small businesses and manufacturers, American workers. And I think that we're going to hopefully still see an aggressive push to make sure that that agriculture has a very solid seat at the table and making sure China falls through with some of the agreements, but also that those agreements get stronger and better. And hopefully we can continue to have significant trade negotiations that lead to agreements with say Vietnam, other Asian countries that could be very helpful, but they need to be appropriate. Some of those tariffs that we have for our agriculture products in these countries are just unacceptable. And our farmers, if we have a level playing field, no one can compete with us. And I think that they know that, and sometimes it's not always helpful, but we also have to look at Europe. Some folks that are supposed to be our strongest allies, When it comes to agriculture trade with them, they're not. And they put in these trade barriers that definitely can hurt our farmers. And we have to be pushing solidly on these trade barriers. I've been meeting with different ambassadors from the European Union, of course, the United Kingdom. And that process is going to continue. But it's still too early to know exactly where President Biden's going to be on a lot of these issues. But right now, it's so far I like who the USTR ambassador is. And I think that that's going to go a long way in pushing forward those policies.",
