    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92294.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "No, I just, I appreciate what you all do at Farm Bureau. I can remember just early on, I see some of the names that are very familiar that I've worked with, even from the state, and now as a member of Congress. Your voice in the halls of Washington and the halls in Jefferson City has been extremely helpful in making sure that the policies that truly affect my bosses, the people that I represent in in Southeast Missouri and who I represented as a state rep. You're a very strong voice for them. And so I appreciate that, Derek. Keep that up. I can't say that about a lot of entities. Sometimes they're blinded by things that's not always in the best interest of their members. You all are not. And so I appreciate that. And it means a lot and happy to be with you.",
